# --- PREDICTION (written for F19 = b5ed5b0d; F20 adds the piruntime launch-exit diagnosis #89 and the D48 ledger data #88, so the same values are predicted to change and BUNDLE, CAL, BASH, NODE to stay). Not a measurement. Basis: git diff b26e5efd b5ed5b0d (35 commits, merge of PR #87 at b5ed5b0d), checked 2026-11-07. ---
# Supervisor non-test code changed (cmd/tbound, cmd/tbound-run, cmd/tbound-profile, cmd/tbound-cell-entrypoint, internal/procoracle, netoracle, runner, broker, evalcorpus, evaluationindex, piruntime).
#   So TBOUND_DIGEST, TBP_DIGEST, ENTRYPOINT_DIGEST and SRC_DIGEST are predicted to change. SRC: the git tree differs (84f5ae8b -> 563949d4).
#   Also predicted to change (inferred): TEST_PROCORACLE (procoracle sources changed), TEST_ENTRYPOINT (cell entrypoint main changed), TBOUND_RUN_DIGEST (cmd/tbound-run changed).
# adapter/ did NOT change (git diff --quiet rc=0), and neither did scripts/prepare_official_pi_runtime.py or packaging/governed/. So BUNDLE_DIGEST is predicted UNCHANGED. BUNDLE takes no commit epoch: its tar is --mtime=@0 (25-p2-rebuild.sh:109) and prepare zeroes mtimes (scripts/prepare_official_pi_runtime.py:427, :611, :616).
# packaging/ changed in one file only: packaging/container/README.md (a doc line). Containerfile and packaging/governed/ did not change.
#   IMGDIGEST still changes: the image carries tbound-cell-entrypoint (changed), and it is built with --epoch = the freeze commit time (30-p3.sh:14, :21): 1794089909 at b5ed5b0d (22:18:29Z), 1794043081 at b26e5efd (09:18:01Z).
#   So IMGDIGEST is predicted to change. Follow-on, inferred: CFG, BASE_TD and LOAD_TAR_DIGEST follow the image.
# CAL_RO_DIGEST and CAL_RW_DIGEST: predicted UNCHANGED (calibration pair, reused in F18; the default 20-r1 mode re-verifies the installed pair).
# BASH_DIGEST and NODE_DIGEST: predicted UNCHANGED (packaging/governed/ is unchanged).
# Measurer pair: launcher_linux.go, host.go and profile_tooling_linux.go (supervisor/internal/piruntime/) are unchanged in b26e5efd..b5ed5b0d (git diff --quiet rc=0 each). So the (b26e5efd, F19) pair is the pinned F18 measurer.
#   supervisor/internal/productdriver/host.go is not the measurer's host.go, and it did not change in this range.
#   Open for the owner: cmd/tbound-profile changed (construct_evidence_linux.go, construct_linux.go, preregistration_linux.go and their tests), outside the three-file measurer set. Confirm that still satisfies the kit's measurer rule (infra/freeze/README.md:46-51) before 05.
